# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-10-ramses-exchange/blob/236e9e9e0cf452828ab82620b6c36c1e6c7bb441/contracts/CL/core/RamsesV3Pool.sol#L152-L174


# Vulnerability details

## Proof of Concept
In Rameses V3 Pool, we will initialize the oracle when we initialize the pool. 
The problem is that we initialize oracle with time =0, this will cause the Observation[0] is initialized with time = 0. This is incorrect. We should initialize this timestamp to block.timestamp.

Ramses provide Oracle, other web3 system will integrate with Ramses's Oracle. They will want to calculate the price via Ramses oracle. If `Observation[0]`'s timestamp is 0, third party web3 system tries to get price via oracle and the `tickCumulative` may be incorrect. This may cause the third party web3 system trigger wrong actions, for example, liquidating users' position which should not be liquidated.

```javascript
    function initialize(uint160 sqrtPriceX96) external {
        PoolStorage.PoolState storage $ = PoolStorage.getStorage();

        if ($.slot0.sqrtPriceX96 != 0) revert AI();

        int24 tick = TickMath.getTickAtSqrtRatio(sqrtPriceX96);
        // @audit here the input time should be timestamp ???
        // Need to double confirm, because they change a lot in oracle part.
@>        (uint16 cardinality, uint16 cardinalityNext) = Oracle.initialize($.observations, 0);
        ...
    }
    function initialize(
        Observation[65535] storage self,
        uint32 time
    ) internal returns (uint16 cardinality, uint16 cardinalityNext) {
        self[0] = Observation({
            blockTimestamp: time,
            tickCumulative: 0,
            secondsPerLiquidityCumulativeX128: 0,
            initialized: true
        });
        return (1, 1);
    }

```
```javascript
    function observeSingle(
        Observation[65535] storage self,
        uint32 time,
        uint32 secondsAgo,
        int24 tick,
        uint16 index,
        uint128 liquidity,
        uint16 cardinality
    ) internal view returns (int56 tickCumulative, uint160 secondsPerLiquidityCumulativeX128) {
        ...
        uint32 target = time - secondsAgo;

        (Observation memory beforeOrAt, Observation memory atOrAfter) =
            getSurroundingObservations(self, time, target, tick, index, liquidity, cardinality);

            // we're in the middle
@>            uint32 observationTimeDelta = atOrAfter.blockTimestamp - beforeOrAt.blockTimestamp;
            uint32 targetDelta = target - beforeOrAt.blockTimestamp;
            return (
                beforeOrAt.tickCumulative +
                    ((atOrAfter.tickCumulative - beforeOrAt.tickCumulative) / observationTimeDelta) *
                    targetDelta,
                beforeOrAt.secondsPerLiquidityCumulativeX128 +
                    uint160(
                        (uint256(
                            atOrAfter.secondsPerLiquidityCumulativeX128 - beforeOrAt.secondsPerLiquidityCumulativeX128
                        ) * targetDelta) / observationTimeDelta
                    )
            );

    }
```
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Initialize oracle with block.timestamp.


## Assessed type

Error

# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-10-ramses-exchange/blob/236e9e9e0cf452828ab82620b6c36c1e6c7bb441/contracts/CL/core/RamsesV3Pool.sol#L152-L174


# Vulnerability details

## Proof of Concept
When we try to initialize one pool, we will initialize the new periods and update the `startTick`.
But the problem is that we call _advancePeriod() at first and then initialize `$.slot0`. It means that the $.slot0 is not initialized when we call _advancePeriod(). This will cause the `_newPeriod.startTick` is zero.


```javascript
    function initialize(uint160 sqrtPriceX96) external {
        PoolStorage.PoolState storage $ = PoolStorage.getStorage();

        if ($.slot0.sqrtPriceX96 != 0) revert AI();

        int24 tick = TickMath.getTickAtSqrtRatio(sqrtPriceX96);
        (uint16 cardinality, uint16 cardinalityNext) = Oracle.initialize($.observations, 0);

@>        _advancePeriod();

        $.slot0 = Slot0({
            sqrtPriceX96: sqrtPriceX96,
            tick: tick,
            observationIndex: 0, // initial index is 0.
            observationCardinality: cardinality,
            observationCardinalityNext: cardinalityNext,
            feeProtocol: 0,
            unlocked: true
        });
    }

    function _advancePeriod() public {
        PoolStorage.PoolState storage $ = PoolStorage.getStorage();

        /// @dev if in new week, record lastTick for previous period
        /// @dev also record secondsPerLiquidityCumulativeX128 for the start of the new period
        uint256 _lastPeriod = $.lastPeriod;
        if ((_blockTimestamp() / 1 weeks) != _lastPeriod) {
            ...
            /// @dev record start tick and secondsPerLiquidityCumulativeX128 for new period
            PeriodInfo memory _newPeriod;

            _newPeriod.previousPeriod = uint32(_lastPeriod);
@>            _newPeriod.startTick = _slot0.tick;
            $.periods[period] = _newPeriod;
        }
    }
```

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
We should initialize $.slot0 and then trigger `_advancePeriod`.





