A malicious user in a griefing attack can continously increase liquduity by as low as 1 wei to continously dos attempt to burn a position.


### Recommended Mitigation Steps

Ways to fix this include
1. Automatically removing liquidity when `burn` is called;
2. Introducing a minimum amount of liquidity that can be added by a non-owner to a position. This will make the attack more expensive and disincentivize it.
