    ...
 @> uint8 feeProtocol;
    ...
}
```

When the factory contract is deployed, the `feeProtocol` is initially set to 80 (specifying 80% of fees are to be paid to the `feeCollector` address)

```solidity
constructor(address accessManager) AccessManaged(accessManager) {
        ...

        /// @dev the initial feeSplit of what is sent to the FeeCollector to be distributed to voters and the treasury
        /// @dev 80% to FeeCollector
 @>     feeProtocol = 80;

        ...
    }
```

But when we look at the `flash` function below for a pool for example, the calculation for capturing the % of the fees that go to the protocol is wrong because it's calculating for 1/n % rather than n%

